    <string name="loaded_audio_summary">Audio: %1$s\nDuration: %2$s</string>
    <string name="ui_help_body">Add Audio\nChoose an MP3 soundtrack. Its name and duration appear below Loaded media; tap them to replace it.\n\nAdd Video/Image\nChoose pictures or videos. Numbered filenames are sorted numerically. Supported pictures include JPG, PNG, WEBP, HEIC, and HEIF.\n\nLoaded media\nEach item shows a thumbnail, its full filename, and media details. Long-press the handle to reorder, use the copy icon to duplicate, or the red trash icon to remove. Long-press a video and choose Edit video sound to add censor beeps or tones.\n\nEdit video sound\nUse the back arrow to return, and the play/pause icon beside the timelines to preview. Pinch to zoom. Tap the audio timeline to place an effect, then drag the effect or its handles to adjust its position and length. The effect replaces the original sound during its duration. Save Settings keeps the changes.\n\nMerge To Video\nSelect 720p or 1080p, horizontal or vertical, and 30 or 60 fps, then choose the output filename and location.\n\nPictures with MP3\nImage time 0 keeps the first picture throughout. Set 1-60 seconds to cycle through pictures until the music ends. With Automatically split time enabled and Image time 0, each picture gets an equal share of the song.\n\nPictures without MP3\nSet Image time to 1-60 seconds. The silent video length is the picture count multiplied by this time.\n\nVideos without MP3\nMultiple videos join in the arranged order, keeping their sound. A single video can repeat 1-60 times; the settings show the estimated length.\n\nPreview and progress\nThe preview shows the selected visual without cropping. MP3 play/pause, seeking, and time appear below it. Merge progress appears above Preview. Status and error messages appear below the playback controls.\n\nBottom buttons\nHelp opens this guide. Application skin selects light or dark. About Us shows the version, contact details, GitHub link, update check, and Read Logs. Every merge appends to Downloads/AVTOHIT/AVTOHIT-debug-log.txt.</string>
